                <pb facs="0164" n="108" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg108"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>The Cabinet Committee on Germany met with Roosevelt on September 6, 1944, and
                    discussed the memoranda prepared by the State, War, and Treasury Departments
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg95">pp. 95</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg98">98</ref>, and <ref target="#pg101">101</ref>, respectively).
                    No official minutes of the meeting have been found, but information on the
                    meeting is included in Hull, p. 1609; Stimson and Bundy, pp. 573–574; and
                    Morgenthau material printed in Blum, pp. 362–363, and <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgenthau Diary</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Germany</hi>), vol. I, pp.
                    536–538.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
